      "title": "Fix Database Seed Issues for Conversations Table",
      "description": "Resolve issues with the database seed script where the db:reset command fails due to a NOT NULL constraint violation on the display_id field in the conversations table.",
      "details": "To fix the database seed issues, first review the current seed script to identify where the display_id field is being set. Ensure that the display_id is generated correctly for each conversation entry. This might involve generating a unique identifier or using a sequence. Additionally, verify that all required fields are populated with valid data to prevent constraint violations. Update the seed script to include mock/demo data checks, ensuring that existing data is not duplicated or overwritten unless necessary. Consider using transactions to ensure atomicity and rollback in case of errors. Test the seed script in a development environment to confirm that it populates the database without errors.",
      "testStrategy": "1. Run the db:reset command in a development environment and ensure it completes without errors. 2. Verify that the conversations table is populated with valid data, including the display_id field. 3. Check that no NOT NULL constraint violations occur during the seeding process. 4. Ensure that mock/demo data checks are functioning correctly by running the seed script multiple times and confirming no duplicate data is created. 5. Review the database logs to ensure no errors or warnings are present during the seeding process.",
      "status": "pending",
